"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[311],{6261:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"Configure","desc":"Configure Struktura runtime options (call before [Struktura.Start]).\\n\\nCurrently supported:\\n- `ServicePromises` (default `true`): when `true`, client service method calls return a Promise-like object.\\n  When `false`, client service method calls synchronously `:await()` and return the result (this yields).","params":[{"name":"options","desc":"","lua_type":"Settings?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":357,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"CreateLifecycle","desc":"Create and (optionally) bind a custom lifecycle event.\\n\\nModules can receive this lifecycle by defining `On<LifecycleName>(...)`.\\nIf Struktura has already started (or is starting), the lifecycle is bound immediately.","params":[{"name":"name","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"signal","desc":"","lua_type":"EventSignal"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Rejects if the lifecycle name already exists.","lua_type":"PromiseLike"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":376,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"CreateSignal","desc":"Create a **signal marker** for use inside a service\'s `Client` table.\\n\\nAt startup, Struktura converts these markers into server signal objects with:\\n- `:Fire(target, ...)`\\n- `:FireAll(...)`\\n- `:FireList(list, ...)`\\n- `:FireExcept(exceptName, ...)`\\n\\nOn the **client**, the same field appears as a signal with `:Connect(callback)` on the proxy returned by [Struktura.GetService].","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":403,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"OnStart","desc":"Returns a Promise that resolves once Struktura has finished starting.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","yields":true,"source":{"line":416,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"Initialize","desc":"Load/register modules from a container folder.\\n\\n- If `deep` is truthy, Struktura scans all descendants; otherwise only direct children.\\n- Modules returning a table are registered as either:\\n  - **Controller** (client): table has `Type == \\"Controller\\"`\\n  - **Service** (server): everything else","params":[{"name":"container","desc":"","lua_type":"Folder"},{"name":"deep","desc":"","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Resolves with a timing string.","lua_type":"PromiseLike"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":440,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"GetController","desc":"Get a previously-initialized controller by name.\\n\\nControllers are registered during [Struktura.Initialize]. Names come from the table\'s `Name` field, or fall back to the ModuleScript name.","params":[{"name":"name","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"T?\\n"}],"function_type":"static","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":467,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"GetService","desc":"Get a service by name.\\n\\n- **Server:** returns the raw service table loaded during [Struktura.Initialize].\\n- **Client:** returns a cached **proxy** built from server metadata.\\n\\nClient proxy behavior:\\n- Signals become objects with `:Connect(callback)`.\\n- Any method call `Service:MethodName(...)` performs a request to the server.\\n\\nUse [Struktura.Configure] to control whether client method calls return a Promise (`ServicePromises = true`) or yield and return directly (`ServicePromises = false`).","params":[{"name":"name","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"T\\n"}],"function_type":"static","realm":["Client","Server"],"yields":true,"source":{"line":508,"path":"src/init.luau"}},{"name":"Start","desc":"Start Struktura.\\n\\nWhat this does:\\n1. Ensures networking is started.\\n2. Binds built-in and custom lifecycles.\\n3. Runs `Init` on every loaded module (services on server / controllers on client).\\n4. **Server only:** surfaces service `Client` APIs (signals + RPC handlers).\\n5. Marks Struktura as started, then runs `Start` for each module.\\n\\nOn the client, Struktura waits for the server to set the `ServerReady` attribute before continuing.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","realm":["Client","Server"],"yields":true,"source":{"line":581,"path":"src/init.luau"}}],"properties":[{"name":"Net","desc":"Low-level networking implementation.\\n\\nMost projects should not interact with this directly. Prefer:\\n- [Struktura.GetService] (client) / [Struktura.GetService] (server)\\n- service `Client` methods\\n- service `Client` signals created via [Struktura.CreateSignal]","lua_type":"any","source":{"line":176,"path":"src/init.luau"}}],"types":[],"name":"Struktura","desc":"Struktura is a lightweight **Services / Controllers** framework for Roblox, with a small networking surface.\\n\\n## How networking works (VoidSentry + Blink)\\n- **Blink** generates the low-level networking modules used by `Struktura.Net` (binary packets over buffers).\\n- **VoidSentry.Dynamic** serializes/deserializes Lua values into a `buffer` that becomes the packet `Payload`.\\n- Struktura builds a friendly API on top: services expose a `Client` surface (methods + signals), and controllers consume it.\\n\\n## Server: Services, client surface, and signals\\nA **Service** is any module that does **not** set `Type = \\"Controller\\"`.\\n\\nIf a service defines a `Client` table:\\n- **Functions** inside `Client` become server RPC handlers callable from the client via [Struktura.GetService].\\n- Fields set to [Struktura.CreateSignal] become server \u2192 client signals (exposed on the client proxy as `:Connect(...)`).\\n\\nFor an example of a Service, you can use this:\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Struktura = require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Struktura)\\n\\nlocal MyService = {\\n\\tName = \\"MyService\\"\\n\\tClient = {\\n\\t\\tDataChanged = Struktura.CreateSignal()\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nfunction MyService.Client:GetData(player: Player...)\\n\\tlocal DataService = Struktura.GetService(\\"DataService\\")\\n\\treturn DataService:GetPlayerData(player)\\nend\\n\\nreturn MyService\\n```\\n\\nOn the client, use [Struktura.GetService] to access these methods and signals.\\n\\nIn this example, [MyService:GetData()] would be accessible on the client, as well as [MyService.DataChanged].\\n\\n## Client: Controllers\\nA **Controller** is any module table with `Type = \\"Controller\\"`.\\n\\nControllers usually:\\n- call [Struktura.GetService] to talk to services\\n- optionally call [Struktura.GetController] to talk to other controllers\\n\\nExample Controller:\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Struktura = require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Struktura)\\n\\nlocal DataController = {\\n\\tName = \\"DataController\\",\\n\\tType = \\"Controller\\",\\n}\\n\\nfunction DataController:Init()\\n\\tself.MyService = Struktura.GetService(\\"MyService\\")\\nend\\n\\nfunction DataController:Start()\\n\\tself.MyService.DataChanged:Connect(function(...)\\n\\t\\tprint(\\"DataChanged:\\", ...)\\n\\tend)\\n\\n\\tself.MyService:GetData():andThen(function(data)\\n\\t\\tprint(\\"GetData result:\\", data)\\n\\tend)\\nend\\n\\nreturn DataController\\n```\\n\\n## Boot\\n1. Call [Struktura.Initialize] to load/register modules.\\n2. Call [Struktura.Start] to run `Init`, surface service `Client` APIs, then run `Start`.","source":{"line":82,"path":"src/init.luau"}}')}}]);